		(property "Design Note" "2.5 V reference, wired as a two-terminal shunt (REF strapped to the cathode). REPLACES the deleted R20 / RV1 / R21 trim divider: POTTING.md section 1.2 (../../../ha/farming/compostlab/o2-probe/) requires the cell to be swappable with the board potted, so no adjustable part may set the bias. AZ431-A datasheet Rev 3.4: B grade is the 0.4% bin, 2.490/2.500/2.510 V, and deviation over -40..85 C is 4.5 mV typ / 10 mV max, so the worst-case window is 2.480..2.520 V. PACKAGE PIN MAP IS NOT THE TI ONE -- N package is 1 REF, 2 CATHODE, 3 ANODE, where TI's TL431DBZ is 1 K, 2 REF, 3 A; see the symbol comment. Biased from +5V_ANALOG through R41 and NOT from 3V3A: the part needs IKA >= 1.0 mA (recommended operating conditions) and 3V3A leaves only 3.234 - 2.510 = 0.724 V of headroom, about 6% margin over that minimum, where +5V_ANALOG leaves 2.5 V"
			(at 0 0 0)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "a9d86850-9732-5d7b-8c00-aa099ae453a9")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
				(justify mirror)
			)
		)
