		(property "MPN" "RC0603FR-071K5L"
			(at 0 0 90)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "bdb16914-9586-5f61-857f-bbaac9aa42de")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
				(justify mirror)
			)
		)
		(property "Design Note" "AZ431 bias resistor, bought to the 1k stock line R33/R36/R37/R38 already carry. Nominal (5.0 - 2.5)/1k = 2.50 mA. WORST CASE, and the first version of this note got it wrong by using the A-grade 2.510 V limit on a B-grade part: U15 is AZ431*B*N, and DS36721 Rev. 6's ordering table is A = 0.4% (2.490-2.510 V), B = 0.8% (2.480-2.520 V). With the 2.520 V limit plus the datasheet's 10 mV deviation over temperature (2.530 V), R41 at +1% (1.010k) and +5V_ANALOG at 4.900 V: (4.900 - 2.530)/1.010k - 2.530/94k = 2.32 mA. BOTH ENDS CHECKED against DS36721 Rev. 6 Recommended Operating Conditions, IKA 1.0 to 100 mA: 2.32 mA clears the floor by 2.3x where 1.5k cleared it by 1.6x, and is 43x under the ceiling. The change ADDS 0.83 mA to +5V_ANALOG (2.50 against 1.67 nominal), which is 8.3 mV more drop across R32=10R; the AP63205's 4.95 V minimum leaves U3 ample headroom for 3.3 V out"
			(at 0 0 90)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "38aea61e-f3ba-5845-bf4c-54bd17a6aca1")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
				(justify mirror)
			)
		)
